/-!
# Simple sections of the even PSU₃ subfield models

The binary model is solvable. Simple quotients of every whole larger
model have constructed carriers, using its faithful primitive action
and solvable point stabilizer. Central and determinant extensions and
strong subfield induction are proved in the imported modules. Proper
overgroups of Sylow 2-subgroups are proved solvable using root generation.

The intrinsic proper-subgroup exhaustion is still required before the
unconditional K-group theorem can be asserted. The conditional theorem
`UnitaryThreeSections.psu3_even_isKGroup_of_exhaustion` retains this exact
remaining premise. Its conclusion includes sections of the whole model,
as required when a PSU₃ group occurs inside a proper PSL₃ subgroup.

Sources: Hartley–Mitchell, GLS3 Theorem 6.5.3, unitary sign in characteristic
two; Aschbacher–Smith, Main Hypothesis 0.1.1(K).
-/
